    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0468" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.61351/126</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-01T23:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 21, 5 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d389-f1"/> After several interviews
                    with Mr. Potter<anchor n="2" xml:id="d389-f2"/> I took him to the President this
                    afternoon. President accepted, without suggesting change, detailed plan for
                    loans prepared by Mr. Potter, and will himself give it official publication. At
                    conference with me, last Saturday, President had accepted plan appointee of
                    bankers or of a United States official joining Cuban Government official in
                    signing storehouse certificates for plantation storehouses. To-day Mr. Potter
                    suggested another plan used here to some extent whereby borrower leases
                    storehouses to lender who remains in charge. Either plan acceptable to the
                    President. Mr. Potter not determined which he prefers. The machinery for either
                    can be inaugurated in a few days.</p>
                <p>Mr. Potter somewhat disturbed by fact that large amounts cheap money from London
                    are coming into this market.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d389-f1" n="1" xml:id="d389-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d389-f2" n="2" xml:id="d389-f2-content">
                <p>Representative of the Cuban Sugar Syndicate Corp. for financing the sugar
                    crop.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
